cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use optika in your research, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: optika
abstract: >-
  optika is a Python library for simulating optical systems, similar to Zemax.
  It raytraces sequential systems of mirrors, refractive glasses, multilayer
  coatings, and diffraction gratings with a variety of ruling spacings and
  profiles, and computes the spectral response and resolution of the system.
  Surfaces are placed in global coordinates, and the field of view and
  entrance pupil are computed from the apertures of the surfaces. Sensor
  models include quantum efficiency, noise, and charge diffusion, and a scene
  can be imaged either by raytracing or with a fast linear forward model.
  Since every parameter can be an array from named-arrays, a whole
  configuration space of designs propagates through the raytrace at once, and
  uncertain parameters carry their uncertainty through to the performance of
  the system.
